id: SceneVariants
name: ᝯㄝₓ Scene Variants
metadata:
  description: "A scene is often in your library twice: the full version and a cut from it. This plugin links them by stash-id and shows them on the scene page.\n\nA scene with other variants gets a Variants tab listing them with cover, preview, resolution and running time. Hover a row to see how that variant differs: the tags it adds or lacks, and which fields disagree. Name your full-duration and partial-duration tags in Tags and Fields, below, and every row is labelled, full-duration first; tags beneath them in your hierarchy count too.\n\nSynchronize Variants pushes this scene's values to its variants. Every difference is listed first, nothing is written until you approve, and Undo works while the dialog stays open. Saving a scene offers the same for what you just changed, unless you switch that off in Scene Page Behaviour, below.\n\nThree tasks keep the sets in order. Migrate Variant Stash-IDs moves the stash-id off partial-duration cuts into a custom field, since a stash-id names the whole work. Flag Variants tags every scene that has variants, so one filter lists them all, and tagging scenes yourself groups them into a new set. Review Variant Sets lists sets by how far their members have drifted apart, worst first.\n\nScene cards show ⸎ and the variant count, and a partial-duration scene gets an Open Full-Duration button. A scene with neither a stash-id nor the variant field has nothing to match against.\n\nRequires Stash 0.31.0 or newer."
